; A 20 x 10 x 2 bar (x 0..20) held at 20 C over its first 0.01 mm, 1 W spread over its last millimetre
; (x 19..20), on 0.2 mm cells. Every datum is uniform over the section and the other faces are insulated, so
; it is exactly one-dimensional: T = 20 + the integral of the flux over k A (k in W/(m K), A 20 mm2).
; k rises 90 to 110 along an arctangent 0.1 mm wide about x 10.42, with a k 1 layer 0.03 mm thick at
; x 10.405..10.435 on it: a layer on a gentle slope.
; truth: cool fails about 31.389 (the 1-D integral, 2e6 steps; 29.904 without the layer)
(import "std")
(def part (move (box 20 10 2) 10 0 0))
(study hot (shape part) (heat (k (* 1W/m/K (select (max (- 10.405 x) (- x 10.435)) 1 (+ 100 (* 6.366197723675814 (atan (/ (- x 10.42) 0.1))))))))
 (temperature cold (- x 0.01) 20degC)
 (source chip (power 1W) (region (- 19 x))) (res 0.2))
(require cool (max-temperature hot < 30.5degC))
